## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:** The sprint column model becomes **`title` + `color` + `status`** (renaming the previous `value`). The `status` is the `chat.status` value written/grouped by the column. If the user doesn't define a status, the **title is used**. When the column's status is edited, the **tasks that were in that column must have their `status` updated** so the cards follow the column.

**Strategic Approach:**
1. Store sprint columns on `board.columns` as `{ id, title, color, status }`.
2. `sprintColumns` getter groups tasks by `t.status === (col.status || col.title)`.
3. Actions gain a `status` field: `addSprintColumn` (status defaults to title, duplicates rejected), `updateSprintColumn` (**migrates the column's tasks when the status changes**), `removeSprintColumn` (migrates on removal). Both `update`/`remove` materialize the default columns first so unedited boards can be edited.
4. `newSprintTask` defaults to the **first column's status** instead of the hard-coded `'todo'`, so custom columns never hide new tasks.
5. Modals: the column dialog gains a sprint-only **Status** input (with a hint), validates duplicate status, and `newTaskStatus` resolves from `column.status`.
6. Canvas/Column/View: switch every `value` reference to `status`.

**Dependencies & Risks:** The shared canvas/column/modal components are also used by kanban. The Status field is gated with `!isKanban`, kanban never sets `status`, and all column actions are sprint-only (kanban still uses its own `addColumn/updateColumn/deleteColumn`). Duplicate status is blocked in both the modal (error message) and the store (no-op) to avoid a task rendering twice.

**Target Files:**
- `src/store/kanban.js` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardCanvas.vue` (modify)

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

