## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:** Give a sprint board column an **`icon`** (Font Awesome), chosen through a **reusable Font Awesome icon selector component**. The icon is stored on the column alongside `title`, `color` and `status`, rendered in the column header, and preserved through add / edit / export / import.

**Strategic Approach**
1. Create a new, self-contained `IconSelector.vue` UI primitive (searchable grid + free-text class entry, dark-first, keyboard/Escape friendly, `v-model` on `update:modelValue`).
2. Extend the sprint column model on the store with `icon`:
   - `defaultSprintColumns()` seeds `icon` from the canonical status icon (keeps current look).
   - `sprintColumns` getter resolves `icon = col.icon || (isStatus ? config.icon : null)` so a user icon overrides the status default, while custom columns fall back to the color dot when empty.
   - `materializeSprintColumns`, `addSprintColumn`, `updateSprintColumn` accept/keep `icon`.
   - `exportBoard` / `importBoard` round-trip `icon`.
3. Wire the selector into the column dialog (`SprintBoardModals.vue`) as a sprint-only field (mirrors the sprint-only `status` field), and pass `icon` through the create/update emits.
4. `SprintBoardView.vue` forwards `icon` to the store actions.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `SprintBoardColumn.vue` **already** renders `column.icon` (with a color-dot fallback) → no change needed there.
- The column dialog & canvas are shared with the kanban board; the icon field is gated with `!isKanban`, so kanban keeps its color-dot behaviour and the kanban store `addColumn/updateColumn` are untouched.
- The selector opens an inline popover (not a nested modal) so it can safely live inside the column modal.

**Target Files**
- `src/components/ui/IconSelector.vue` (new)
- `src/store/kanban.js` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` (modify)
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` (modify)

---

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

| File | Change surface |
| :--- | :--- |
| `src/components/ui/IconSelector.vue` | New component. Curated catalog + search + free-text class input. |
| `src/store/kanban.js` | 7 small edits: defaults, getter, 3 sprint-column actions, export, import. No existing behaviour removed. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardModals.vue` | Import + one field (`newColumn.icon`) + one template block + 3 payload spots. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardView.vue` | 2 handlers forward `icon`. |

---

## 3. Design specification (IconSelector)

| Aspect | Spec |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Trigger** | `btn-sm btn-ghost`, `border-base-100`, shows current icon chip + class label + chevron. Signals state via `aria-expanded`. |
| **Panel** | `rounded-box`, `bg-base-200`, `border-base-100`, `shadow-xl`, `z-50`, anchored `top-full`. |
| **Search** | `input-xs`, magnifier prefix, `Esc` closes. |
| **Grid** | `grid-cols-8`, `aspect-square` targets, `hover:bg-base-300`, selected = `bg-primary text-primary-content`. |
| **Groups** | 10 labelled groups (Status · Tasks & Planning · Code & Dev · Files & Data · Communication · People & Teams · Time · Analytics · Design · General). |
| **Free text** | Fallback input accepting any FA class (`fa-solid fa-star`, `fa-brands fa-trello`, bare `star`). |
| **Accessibility** | `aria-label`, `aria-expanded`, visible focus (DaisyUI buttons), `title` on each cell, `Escape` to close. |

---

