## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core requirements**
- Every board column must render its icon the **same way**: a **circle** filled with the column's **background colour** and the **icon centred** inside it.
- Today the shared column header (`SprintBoardColumn.vue`) has **two different renderings**:
  - columns **with an icon** (canonical sprint statuses → *"On Hold"* shows `fa-circle-pause` in `text-warning/60`, no background);
  - columns **without an icon** → a tiny 2px colour dot (custom/kanban columns).

**Strategic approach**
- Unify both branches into a single reusable "badge": a `w-5 h-5 rounded-full` circle that always contains *something* in the middle (the icon, or a small colour dot when the column defines none).
- Colour source for the circle:
  - **custom / kanban columns** → the colour picked in the column dialog (hex, applied inline);
  - **canonical sprint statuses** (`todo · doing · onhold · done · rejected`) → the project's semantic tokens (`bg-warning/20 text-warning`, …), which match what the rest of the app already uses (`border-l-warning`, `text-warning/60`, …).
- Custom colours are applied with a low-opacity layer + solid icon colour, so the badge stays legible over any board background image.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- Single-file change; no store/API/contract impact. The `column.textColor` prop stays present (still used by the modals) — only its use *inside the header icon* is dropped in favour of the solid token.
- Literal Tailwind classes are written in the component source, so the JIT scanner generates `bg-*/20` variants regardless of other usages.
- Icon-less columns keep the colour-dot information (now centred inside the circle instead of a bare 2px dot).

**Target files**
- `src/components/kanban/board/SprintBoardColumn.vue` → *modify* (unified circular icon badge).

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach

**`SprintBoardColumn.vue`** — replace the two-branch header icon (status `<i>` / colour `<span>`) with one circular badge; add the status→token map + a `columnBadgeClass` computed. Everything else (header, drag handling, task list, watchers, methods) is untouched.

